WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.120
It's no secret we love some drama, right?

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:08.320
Oh, how nice to follow a story of inspiration
and friendship like the one between

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:13.760
two of the night's big nominees,
Olivia Rodrigo and Taylor Swift.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:19.880
Since breaking out in January 2021,
Olivia has made it crystal clear Tay-Tay

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.640
was one of her big inspirations,
if not the biggest.

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:26.360
Ever since she was mini Olivia, okay?

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.700
Here, for example, she's literally
campaigning and holding a sign:

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:32.280
"I love Taylor Swift."

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:37.479
So just imagine how Liv felt
about Taylor's fangirl moment.

00:00:37.519 --> 00:00:39.680
It was so cute.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:44.600
When Drivers License debuted at No. 1
on the Billboard Hot 100, Olivia posted

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:49.560
about it on Insta and Taylor commented:
"I'm like, that's my baby, I'm so proud."

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:53.800
To which Olivia replied:
"Crying like a baby.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.200
Thank you for everything you do."

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:00.920
With the release of Sour, Olivia's
debut album, lots of fans of the duo

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.760
noticed the similarity between 1 Step
Forward, 3 Steps Back and New Year's Day

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:10.360
by Tay-Tay. And Olivia confirmed that
yes, she'd used the arrangements of New

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:14.720
Year's Day as inspiration for the track,
with Taylor's approval, by the way,

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:18.720
okay? And she even added Taylor
Swift to the credits of Deja Vu for

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:23.160
sounding like the track Cruel
Summer, from the album Lover.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:26.400
I mean, she shares the joy
and she splits the dough.

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:31.040
And just like with drama, with
friendship we also ask: "So, what's up,

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:33.420
girls? Where's the collab?"
